README.md:1:# ProAI Expert Website
README.md:2:
README.md:3:A bilingual studio website for ProAI Expert, built as a clean static site with parallel English and Russian content layers.
README.md:4:
README.md:5:The project brings together practical AI systems, business automation, premium websites, branding, and digital business structure for modern service businesses.
README.md:6:
README.md:7:## Positioning
README.md:8:
README.md:9:ProAI Expert is a studio working across:
README.md:10:
README.md:11:- practical AI systems
README.md:12:- business automation
README.md:13:- premium websites
README.md:14:- branding
README.md:15:- digital business structure
README.md:16:
README.md:17:The site is designed to present these directions as one coherent studio offering rather than as disconnected services.
README.md:18:
README.md:19:## Website Structure
README.md:20:
README.md:21:The core website includes:
README.md:22:
README.md:23:- Home
README.md:24:- About
README.md:25:- AI Systems
README.md:26:- Websites & Branding
README.md:27:- Contact
README.md:28:- Insights
README.md:29:- Insight article pages
README.md:30:
README.md:31:The Insights layer includes editorial hub pages plus article pages in both languages.
README.md:32:
README.md:33:## Bilingual Structure
README.md:34:
README.md:35:The site uses a language-specific folder structure:
README.md:36:
README.md:37:- English pages live at the root (`/`)
README.md:38:- Russian pages live under `/ru/`
README.md:39:- English Insights content lives under `/insights/`
README.md:40:- Russian Insights content lives under `/ru/insights/`
README.md:41:
README.md:42:The Russian and English versions are language-specific adaptations. They are not intended to be crude mirror translations.
README.md:43:
README.md:44:## Repository Structure
README.md:45:
README.md:46:Key project paths:
README.md:47:
README.md:48:- `/` — English root pages
README.md:49:- `/ru/` — Russian root pages
README.md:50:- `/insights/` — English Insights hub and article pages
README.md:51:- `/ru/insights/` — Russian Insights hub and article pages
README.md:52:- `sitemap.xml` — sitemap for search engines
README.md:53:- `robots.txt` — crawl and sitemap directives
README.md:54:
README.md:55:## Current Content Layer
README.md:56:
README.md:57:The current site already includes:
README.md:58:
README.md:59:- all main pages in English and Russian
README.md:60:- Insights hub pages in English and Russian
README.md:61:- the first flagship article set in both languages
README.md:62:  - 3 Russian articles
README.md:63:  - 3 English articles
README.md:64:
README.md:65:## Editing Guidance
README.md:66:
README.md:67:Use the existing folder structure consistently.
README.md:68:
README.md:69:- Edit root pages directly inside the corresponding folder
README.md:70:- Edit Russian pages inside `/ru/`
README.md:71:- Add English articles inside `/insights/<slug>/`
README.md:72:- Add Russian articles inside `/ru/insights/<slug>/`
README.md:73:
README.md:74:When updating content:
README.md:75:
README.md:76:- keep English and Russian parity thoughtful, not literal
README.md:77:- avoid random renaming of folders or files
README.md:78:- avoid structure drift between language layers
README.md:79:- preserve clean version progression across release archives
README.md:80:
README.md:81:## Deployment Note
README.md:82:
README.md:83:This is a static website suitable for GitHub Pages or comparable static hosting.
README.md:84:
README.md:85:Before deployment, verify:
README.md:86:
README.md:87:- internal links
README.md:88:- sitemap
README.md:89:- robots.txt
README.md:90:- canonical and hreflang logic
README.md:91:- contact form behavior
README.md:92:
README.md:93:## Versioning Note
README.md:94:
README.md:95:The project uses sequential ZIP / version naming to keep releases clean and traceable.
README.md:96:
README.md:97:Recommended practice:
README.md:98:
README.md:99:- keep one clear version line
README.md:100:- avoid parallel inconsistent copies
README.md:101:- treat the latest approved archive as the working source
README.md:102:
README.md:103:## Current Status
README.md:104:
README.md:105:The site is in a refined pre-launch state.
README.md:106:
README.md:107:Current work already covers:
README.md:108:
README.md:109:- bilingual main pages
README.md:110:- bilingual Insights hubs
README.md:111:- first bilingual flagship article set
README.md:112:- launch-oriented cleanup of sitemap, robots, canonical / hreflang, and internal links
README.md:113:
README.md:114:## Next Steps
README.md:115:
README.md:116:Likely next steps include:
README.md:117:
README.md:118:- final launch checks
README.md:119:- performance optimization
README.md:120:- additional Insights articles
README.md:121:- ongoing SEO refinement
README.md:122:- visual polish and selective front-end enhancements
